{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"73486ce9-023c-4390-a652-7bcd99a09eff","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Light changes direction when it crosses between materials. We measure each angle from the dashed normal, not the boundary.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Snell's law"},{"op":"diagram","id":"boundary","region":"right","primitives":[{"kind":"line","points":[[0.08,0.5],[0.92,0.5]],"stroke":"solid","label":"boundary"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.5,0.12],[0.5,0.9]],"stroke":"dashed","label":"normal"},{"kind":"text","at":[0.78,0.23],"content":"air: n = 1.00"},{"kind":"text","at":[0.23,0.8],"content":"glass: n = 1.50"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"73486ce9-023c-4390-a652-7bcd99a09eff","step":{"id":"s2","script":"This ray enters glass at forty-five degrees. Because glass has a higher refractive index, the transmitted ray bends toward the normal.","ops":[{"op":"arrow","id":"incident","canvas_id":"boundary","from":[0.18,0.18],"to":[0.5,0.5],"stroke":"solid","label":"incident"},{"op":"arrow","id":"transmitted","canvas_id":"boundary","from":[0.5,0.5],"to":[0.687,0.85],"stroke":"solid","label":"transmitted"},{"op":"angle_arc","id":"incoming_angle","canvas_id":"boundary","center":[0.5,0.5],"radius":0.18,"start_deg":-135,"end_deg":-90,"stroke":"solid","label":"45°"},{"op":"angle_arc","id":"outgoing_angle","canvas_id":"boundary","center":[0.5,0.5],"radius":0.22,"start_deg":61.9,"end_deg":90,"stroke":"solid","label":"θ₂"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"73486ce9-023c-4390-a652-7bcd99a09eff","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s3"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"73486ce9-023c-4390-a652-7bcd99a09eff","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Snell's law connects the two angles through the refractive indices. Substitute the known incident angle and material values.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"snell","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"n_1\\sin\\theta_1=n_2\\sin\\theta_2"},{"op":"equation","id":"substitute","anchor":{"el":"snell","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"1.00\\sin45^\\circ=1.50\\sin\\theta_2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"73486ce9-023c-4390-a652-7bcd99a09eff","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Solving gives about twenty-eight degrees, measured from the normal. The smaller angle confirms bending toward the normal.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"solve","anchor":{"el":"substitute","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\theta_2=\\sin^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{1.00}{1.50}\\sin45^\\circ\\right)\\approx28.1^\\circ"},{"op":"point","id":"ray_value","canvas_id":"boundary","at":[0.687,0.85],"label":"28.1° from normal"}],"checkpoint":null}}
